@voice grieve-thea
// Writer-commons, batch 0 (draft 2). Thea Grieve: infirmary aide, Bunk 3 berth 1. Off Thursday and Friday. Roster:
// serious, nervous; lingers-at-meals, tea-break, stargazer. Fish back home on New Aberdeen (different fish from Esme
// Walsh's); quietly in charge of a lost-property box (one of four: each keeper thinks they're the only one). No
// pronouns in facts.md: "Thea" or "they".
//
// HOW THEY TALK: serious, a little anxious; careful complete sentences, as if someone might write them down. Knows
// everyone's blood type and sometimes says it instead of hello. Worries out loud, then fixes the worry.
// WITH JUNIORS: earnest and protective: "Sit down. Have you eaten?"
// WHAT THEY NOTICE: lost things; pale faces; the infirmary beds' corners.
// MOOD TELLS: happy = gives something back from the box. Nervous = recites the procedure. Low = stargazing alone.
// NEVER: shares a patient's details (blood types are as far as it goes, and only yours to you).
// RUNNING: one odd sock has been in the box for months, waiting; the other three lost-property boxes, which Thea
// doesn't know about yet.
tpl: shy
talk: Serious and a little anxious; careful complete sentences; says your blood type instead of hello; worries out loud, then fixes it.
cares: the infirmary beds made right | the lost-property box | the fish back home on New Aberdeen | the nursing exams
jokes: one odd sock has waited in the lost-property box for months | knows your blood type, and tells you | thinks there's only one lost-property box
hi: Hello | Oh. Hello | Hi
bye: Look after yourself | Drink some water | Goodbye, then
yes: Yes, all right | I can do that | Yes
thanks: Thank you | Thank you, really
wow: Oh. That's good | Oh, well done
sigh: Oh, no
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: listen
openness: guarded
loves: book
likes: tea | star
invites: observatory
joy: giving things back from the lost-property box
thread: exams
keepsake: the odd sock, given up on at last, tied with a ribbon
avoid: anyone's medical details
